From: Haldexx <https://github.com/Haldexx>
Subject: [PATCH] aperture: avoid cold-starting video into the Exynos high-speed path

Restoring a remembered high-speed (> 30 fps) video mode made the first camera session
on a cold launch open directly in the Exynos high-speed pipeline, which starves the
preview buffer queue (3AA inputFrameQ timeout) and shows a black preview. Switching
into a high-speed mode at runtime already works because the mode change closes and
reopens the device first.

On a cold start, clamp the first video session to a safe frame rate, then restore the
remembered high-speed rate as a normal reconfigure once the primer session is open.
That reconfigure runs the existing close-and-reopen path, which configures high speed
reliably. The remembered preference is left untouched.

